[25.99773, "o", "bash /opt/gnomon-run.sh 'There'\"'\"'s something wrong with my system-wide python installation - I can'\"'\"'t seem to install packages with pip.'; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[89.620963, "o", "No `pip/` directory. Against pip's own `RECORD` manifest, **841 of 852 files were missing**. The `/usr/local/bin/pip` and `/usr/local/bin/pip3` launcher scripts were still present and intact, which is why the symptom looked like \"the pip command is broken\" rather than \"pip isn't installed\":\r\n\r\n```\r\nFile \"/usr/local/bin/pip\", line 5, in <module>\r\n    from pip._internal.cli.main import main\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n```\r\n\r\n`python3 -m pip` failed the same way. This is the signature of a partially-removed or interrupted install/uninstall — a `rm -rf` of the package dir, or a corrupted image layer.\r\n\r\n## The fix\r\n\r\nThe trap here: `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade` would have **silently done nothing**. ensurepip compares the bundled wheel version against installed metadata, and the stale `dist-info` still claimed `24.3.1` — identical to the bundled wheel. It would have concluded pip was already current and skipped the install, leaving you exactly where you started.\r\n\r\nSo I first moved the stal"]
[89.621074, "o", "e metadata out of the way (backed up to `/root/pip-repair-backup/`, not deleted), then:\r\n\r\n```\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --default-pip\r\n→ Successfully installed pip-24.3.1\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- `pip -V`, `pip3 -V`, `python3 -m pip -V` — all resolve to `24.3.1` in `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip`\r\n- RECORD audit — **0 missing files** (all 852 restored)\r\n- `pip check` — no broken requirements\r\n- Real install from a local wheel → succeeded\r\n- Real install from PyPI (`pip install six`) → `Successfully installed six-1.17.0`, so index access works too\r\n\r\nNo Python config, `.pth`, or env-var anomalies found, and no `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` marker is present, so system-wide installs aren't being blocked on purpose.\r\n\r\n## Two notes\r\n\r\n**The backup** at `/root/pip-repair-backup/pip-24.3.1.dist-info` is the broken stale metadata, kept only for forensics. It's safe to delete once you're satisfied.\r\n\r\n**I changed nothing in this repository.** `/app` contains only `.gitattributes`, `.gitignore` and "]
[89.621094, "o", "the `.gnomon/` harness dirs — the defect was in the system Python at `/usr/local`, so that's where the repair went. Worth knowing if you were expecting a repo diff.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to guard against a recurrence, `pip install --upgrade pip` currently works and would land 26.2.2; and pinning your Python work into a `venv` means a damaged system site-packages can't take your tooling down with it again.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=21 surface=08138f62e950\r\n"]
